</section></score></mdiv></body>
<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>As in the dawning, o’er the waveless ocean,</l><l>The image of the morning star doth rest,</l><l>So in this stillness Thou beholdest only</l><l>Thine image in the waters of my breast.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>When sinks the soul, subdued by toil, to slumber,</l><l>Its closing eye looks up to Thee in prayer;</l><l>Sweet the repose, beneath Thy wings o’ershadowing,</l><l>But sweeter still to wake and find Thee there.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>So shall it be at last, in that bright morning</l><l>When the soul waketh, and life’s shadows flee;</l><l>Oh, in that hour, fairer than daylight’s dawning,</l><l>Shall rise the glorious thought, I am with Thee!</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
